{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1000435-bit-of-a-controversial-subject-world-of-darkness-and-politics","id":1000435,"title":"Bit of a Controversial Subject: World of Darkness and Politics","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-08T14:27:12-08:00","id":1000435,"title":"Bit of a Controversial Subject: World of Darkness and Politics","content":"I dont mean camarilla, sabbat, tribal politics or Chantry politics.<br /> <br /> Im curious about how does the WoD reacts to certain individuals such as Tatcher, Nixon, Clinton etc... the Democrat and Republican party and so on.<br /> <br /> personally im quite curious to know about how do british mages went around when it was the time of Margaret Tatcher (I dont know if the OoH was on her side, or if they didnt cared)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T16:34:45-08:00","id":1000507,"title":"","content":"Vampires (at least the elders) really like a strong difference between rich and poor. There's not much a vampire can do if everyone earns $60k and lives in a nice house. The obscenely rich offer a great deal of entertainment, and the really poor offer a great feeding ground where nobody asks questions if someone goes missing. <br /> <br /> <br /> Camarilla elders, quite happily, are great fans of racism. Apparently, sabbat are more ethnically diverse than camarilla, so instilling a good bit of racism into the populace can cause a good plan to go awry when a sabbat gets called out for his race, frenzies, and attention is drawn. Though this information isn't really something those elders are happy to share with the idealistic neonates. <br /> <br /> Werewolves? <br /> Bernie sanders would have saved america. The total opposite of vampires. Maybe some werewolves will be happy with a socialist system,since the above vampire strategy really encourages the wyrm (even if socialism would arguably strengthen the weaver) but some tribes (shadow lords, silver fangs, Glass walkers, bone gnawers) have varied interest in how economics work and favour. <br /> <br /> Mages? <br /> Syndicate- Free market capitalists, probably.<br /> NWO- Probably socialist. <br /> Technocracy in general- Anything that favours science.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Signatures are for terrible people who want to be caught.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12414-flower-innocent","name":"Flower,Innocent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T16:44:52-08:00","id":1000517,"title":"","content":"The official word is generally that mortal politics is decided by mortals, because saying that a particular politician or movement is influenced by supernatural beings is likely to cause offence. It's less of an issue with time, which is why various books offer suggestions on how to use the real-life strange rumours about Rasputin for example, but for more modern individuals it's left to individual Storytellers to make decisions about what's really going on in their setting.<br /> <br /> Nixon is probably distant enough now to feature in asides about various supernatural groups accusing each other of influencing him because none of them would admit to it themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T18:35:03-08:00","id":1000572,"title":"","content":"I give this thread a maximum of one day before it goes to shit...and that's optimistic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T18:49:32-08:00","id":1000575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1000435-bit-of-a-controversial-subject-world-of-darkness-and-politics?p=1000572#post1000572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I give this thread a maximum of one day before it goes to shit...and that's optimistic.</div> </div> </div> </div>4 posts after this and im being kind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T19:07:44-08:00","id":1000581,"title":"","content":"Well, I don't think it will go to shit so quickly, considering how things usually are on this forum.<br /> <br /> I call 3 days.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1000435-bit-of-a-controversial-subject-world-of-darkness-and-politics#post1000435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dont mean camarilla, sabbat, tribal politics or Chantry politics.<br /> <br /> Im curious about how does the WoD reacts to certain individuals such as Tatcher, Nixon, Clinton etc... the Democrat and Republican party and so on.<br /> <br /> personally im quite curious to know about how do british mages went around when it was the time of Margaret Tatcher (I dont know if the OoH was on her side, or if they didnt cared)</div> </div> </div> </div>This is an interesting question, if one that ultimately can be answered only in play, by you and your friends. If it works for you.<br /> <br /> Supposedly, most of the characters on WoD are quite into mortal politics. It isn't further discussed in the books to avoid obvious hazards, and for similar reasons, or simple disinterest, most groups don't pay it any attention either. But at least on the background of the setting, we can see the relation is actually intense.<br /> <br /> A vampire have an invested interest on how the city is. First because it affects her feelings and beliefs. Second because it directly affects her unlife. It affects her food and her shelter, her possessions, her context, and her (hidden) society. Vampires are specially used to become big, if hidden, players at a local level, so city politics is an intimate part of their unlives. They will be connected, they will be influential, in as many circles as they can. They will try to make a difference, be it for personal or altruistic interest. And since state and country politics can affect their cities, with far less intimacy they can still have invested interests on most of it.<br /> <br /> Werewolves have an interesting relation with politics. On the most part, they try as much as they can to stay at large of mortal society. But their interests are too frequently linked to politics. Some try to ignore it, but others become very involved on said politics. Environmental groups, ethnic questions, protected sites. The purview of interests of the Garou Nation too frequently crosses with political issues.<br /> <br /> Mage goes a step further. Belief is their bread and butter, in a too literal sense. The Technocratic Union is a huge Conspiracy, the kind that have some of the greatest legends of world-spanning conspiracies as just factions of them, like the New World Order and the $yndicate (the Gnomes of Zurich). The Traditions fight yet, if loosing it, an Ascension War with the ultimate prize as the Consensus, the collective belief of humanity. Politics everywhere, on their intent, as their weapon, as their shield, religion, science and politics are their very medium for the true fight. And if you get this out of the way, a single Mage is still a being of Paradigm. It means that belief shapes her magic and her life. Most will go to any length for their beliefs, because such disposition is what made them Mages to begin with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T16:26:17-08:00","id":1001059,"title":"","content":"The political system reflects a struggle between the Syndicate and the New World Order. The Syndicate are capitalists and support the free reign of big business and more or less free markets, where as the NWO are socialists and prefer a government controlled economy. Of course, all modern political movements and systems are heavily influenced by the Technocracy, but the people's opinion can influence what flavor of Technocracy that they get.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T18:38:44-08:00","id":1001126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1000435-bit-of-a-controversial-subject-world-of-darkness-and-politics?p=1001059#post1001059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The political system reflects a struggle between the Syndicate and the New World Order. The Syndicate are capitalists and support the free reign of big business and more or less free markets, where as the NWO are socialists and prefer a government controlled economy. Of course, all modern political movements and systems are heavily influenced by the Technocracy, but the people's opinion can influence what flavor of Technocracy that they get.</div> </div> </div> </div>And here it is. The above post about &quot;mortals decide mortal politics&quot; gets ruined by Mage, since it doesn't so much as try to stick its fingers in the &quot;supernatural conspiracies are about!&quot; pie as much as it does dive into a comparably-themed tub of pudding and make a mess of everything forever after, refusing to clean itself off or see anything as amiss with the way it sets things up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T10:18:12-08:00","id":1001397,"title":"","content":"lets look at this by splat- (these are all general impressions. exceptions exist all over)<br /> Mage- heavily political. battling for the minds of humanity is inevitably going to get political. its one of the major battlefronts of the ascension war. the technocracy is presented as having their fingers in government science and law. its actually hard to avoid politics with the technocrats.<br /> Werewolf- marginally political. the battle here is in the umbra where essence and emotion hold sway. wolves in the cities may get involved in politics but if they really had that much of a grip in human society Pentex would never have been allowed to be a thing. Pentex is presented as a battlefront catching the werewolves unprepared.<br /> Vampire- fairly political. vampires want to influence humans but their actions are more like chess moves especially since they only get to come out to play after everyone's gone to bed. wake up, review the news, mindblast certain politicians and police to make them obey your will, wait till next night to see how it played out. rinse and repeat.<br /> Changeling- hardly political. politics is likely to be highly baniel to changelings and while some may try to fight against city hall many changelings are far more interested in kicking around chimerical dragons than getting legal bills to pass.<br /> Wraith- mildly political. wraiths are interested in local events onlysofar as they affect their passions and fetters. who cares who is in office when specters are breathing down your neck after the latest malestrom.<br /> Demon- eventualy political. Demons want power and they are going to go after influential thralls pretty quickly in their 10 point plan to conquer heaven and earth","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>there are no bad ideas, just ideas that have not been refined enough","edited":{"userid":1608,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1608-iamthesweeper","user":"IAmTheSweeper","date":". 11-10-2016, 01:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1608-iamthesweeper","name":"IAmTheSweeper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1608_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T12:07:41-08:00","id":1001419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IAmTheSweeper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1000435-bit-of-a-controversial-subject-world-of-darkness-and-politics?p=1001397#post1001397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolf- marginally political. the battle here is in the umbra where essence and emotion hold sway. wolves in the cities may get involved in politics but if they really had that much of a grip in human society Pentex would never have been allowed to be a thing. Pentex is presented as a battlefront catching the werewolves unprepared.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pentex is only one organization of antagonists that do this. There are also WICs that aren't under its umbrella, governmental bodies, housing compacts, and all manner of social bodies that aren't readily just stamped out by a rampage, no matter how surgical. Additionally, Pentex is merely squatting on an endemic and deep-seated cultural problem, so it isn't even the ultimate cause that has to be fought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T12:25:55-08:00","id":1001427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1000435-bit-of-a-controversial-subject-world-of-darkness-and-politics?p=1001059#post1001059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The political system reflects a struggle between the Syndicate and the New World Order. The Syndicate are capitalists and support the free reign of big business and more or less free markets, where as the NWO are socialists and prefer a government controlled economy. Of course, all modern political movements and systems are heavily influenced by the Technocracy, but the people's opinion can influence what flavor of Technocracy that they get.</div> </div> </div> </div>Was going to say just this, its part of the reason the NWO and Syndicate are always arguing with each other. But more to the point Mage goes after political parties so they can change people perceptions while Vampires would go after non-elected bureaucrats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9486-jbrocky","name":"JBRocky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9486_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T12:59:18-08:00","id":1001445,"title":"","content":"In general I think that most vampires and Pentex would tend to focus more on the state and local governments than the national government. Due to difficulties with operating directly in person (sunlight, travel, etc) most vampires who dabble in politics probably won't invest heavily in national politics. At most a vampire might try to help back a member of Congress in exchange for the Congressman giving that vampire's community various pork or red meat type initiatives. Vampires might donate money to national candidates, but in general I can't imagine most of them being terribly interested in doing so. <br /> <br /> Pentex would also tend to focus on the local and state level. Buying off state and local politicians is a lot cheaper than federal ones, and those are the guys you need to bribe to get around zoning restrictions, avoid local investigations, etc. <br /> <br /> The Technocracy would meddle in national affairs - their goal is mastery of humanity as a whole, and being able to steer a country like America lets them (to a degree) steer the world. <br /> <br /> Still, for the most part I suspect that there is little direct supernatural meddling in most major, national elections - it's easy to imagine Pentex or a local Prince engaging in various tactics (fraud, bullying, voter intimidation, etc) to get a specific politician elected, but those kind of tactics don't really work on the national level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T13:20:30-08:00","id":1001458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1000435-bit-of-a-controversial-subject-world-of-darkness-and-politics?p=1001445#post1001445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In general I think that most vampires and Pentex would tend to focus more on the state and local governments than the national government. Due to difficulties with operating directly in person (sunlight, travel, etc) most vampires who dabble in politics probably won't invest heavily in national politics. At most a vampire might try to help back a member of Congress in exchange for the Congressman giving that vampire's community various pork or red meat type initiatives. Vampires might donate money to national candidates, but in general I can't imagine most of them being terribly interested in doing so.<br /> <br /> Pentex would also tend to focus on the local and state level. Buying off state and local politicians is a lot cheaper than federal ones, and those are the guys you need to bribe to get around zoning restrictions, avoid local investigations, etc.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy would meddle in national affairs - their goal is mastery of humanity as a whole, and being able to steer a country like America lets them (to a degree) steer the world.<br /> <br /> Still, for the most part I suspect that there is little direct supernatural meddling in most major, national elections - it's easy to imagine Pentex or a local Prince engaging in various tactics (fraud, bullying, voter intimidation, etc) to get a specific politician elected, but those kind of tactics don't really work on the national level.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pentex, or rather its subsidiaries, don't quite count as &quot;supernatural influence&quot;, since they're corporations that tend to be overwhelmingly human.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T14:51:35-08:00","id":1001505,"title":"","content":"Yup, Pentex is more about the mortal politics getting into the supernatural than the other way around. And that probably goes a lot with other supernatural phenomena, too. I can easily thinking of a lot of politics looking into the supernatural for advantages. And getting it.<br /> <br /> Werewolf seems like a game of low politics, but there is the trick: the characters are already too powerful at fights and Umbra-stuff, and yet they're loosing. They're loosing because the greater battlefields of this war aren't about brawl or magic. So the political realm is where most of the real challenge is, and the werewolves have to adapt. It isn't that they can't use their brawl and magic, but that they have to contextualize it, or they'll loose. A lot of Garou are loosing because of this. And a lot are adapting. You'll see that Werewolf's official NPCs are almost always involved with politics and/or political issues.<br /> <br /> But I disagree that $yndicate and N.W.O. are capitalists vs socialists. It is to oversimplify both those economic systems and those Conventions. For me, both Liberalism and Socialism are experiments the two Conventions made together (being systems that mingle political system and economic system). Socialism isn't as anti-capitalist as it argues, though it is meant to control capitalism. Money is still the economic basis of it. Capitalism doesn't have to be about <u>free</u> money. Indeed, it is still the greatest achievement of the $yndicate (a system where money lets you lubricate the logistical problems of any endeavor to an extraordinary degree).<br /> <br /> Two days already. This thread is enduring...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T20:50:46-08:00","id":1001613,"title":"","content":"Mages.<br /> <br /> Mages are mortals. <br /> Mages don't have anything on them that changes how they interact with normal people (say perhaps a little fluff about how they get a little more isolated from people subconciously aware of the difference, but that's nothing to rage or being undead) They don't have rage, they can go about in the day. They don't feed from people, they don't shatter minds through revealing true forms, and they're &quot;vincible&quot;, they don't have the physical confidence that gives the social difference a vampire or werewolf might have. <br /> <br /> Mages are the one group in world of darkness that we can simply define as mortal+ (well, sorcerers, psychics and to a lesser extent offshots like kinfolk can be similarly defined) So... well... Their interest in mortal politics is the same as any other humans would be. The NWO and Syndicate? About the same level as very influential corporations and lobbyists in terms of politics. Itteration X and progenitors are to a large extent just research groups. Traditions can be likened to hobbyists, organisations or whatever. <br /> <br /> Mages don't have political opinions by virtue of being a mage. People are mages, and they just happen to have this view and fit in with this group. The difference between a person with an ideology and a mage with an ideology is magick, their political opinions aren't significantly affected by it. <br /> <br /> A Werewolf, by contrast, Will have the political state of things affect the environment and can potentially spill into the umbra. This affects their relations with spirits. Furthermore, Garou society is highly segregated from normal humans because of rage, delerium and the veil. This allows them to huddle up together and foster more extreme opinions that are unchecked by wider society. It is in their best interest to not only protect the environment from polution, but to keep the populace happy and free of wyrmish influences. <br /> <br /> A vampire needs to feed and keep herself entertained. She needs to control the herd and shape it to suit her. Policies dicatate who's on the streets and on the menu, and how much they can get away with. The more corrupt the system, the easier it is for vampires. Poorer neighborhoods are more forgiving, homeless are tasty, the rich offer entertainment. <br /> <br /> But, back to mages. They don't have any such needs. Most of them don't visit the umbra to see what problems werewolves are facing, and none of them need blood, fear sunlight, or are emotionally dead. Mages can do incredible things, but they're largely things that people can do with a bit more spruce in them. A progenitor is going to have cooler things in his lab than just any old biological science guy, but they're not going to be very different otherwise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Signatures are for terrible people who want to be caught.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12414-flower-innocent","name":"Flower,Innocent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T21:10:14-08:00","id":1001619,"title":"","content":"Oh im trying to decide in my own WTA Game on a good local official in Seattle, for a kinfolk to have recently assasinated and the SAD is coming to investigate.a murder carried out under seemingly impossible circumstances<br /> <br /> Im trying to decide who the person was, were they a pawn of the wyrm, or just a well meaning civic official &quot;Who knew too much&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T12:50:50-08:00","id":1001885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1000435-bit-of-a-controversial-subject-world-of-darkness-and-politics?p=1001619#post1001619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh im trying to decide in my own WTA Game on a good local official in Seattle, for a kinfolk to have recently assasinated and the SAD is coming to investigate.a murder carried out under seemingly impossible circumstances<br /> <br /> Im trying to decide who the person was, were they a pawn of the wyrm, or just a well meaning civic official &quot;Who knew too much&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm lets see make it a Federal Position so SAD does get involved, so lets say the Chief of Staff for the local Congressman in Washington.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9486-jbrocky","name":"JBRocky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9486_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T22:20:36-08:00","id":1002120,"title":"","content":"One complicating factor for vampires is the 1940s Decree of the Brujah Justicar that the Prince of DC is not to interfere in Federal Affairs. So there's very much a push from the Justicars and the Council to keep shit small or at least controlled by them, not by local princes. I can dig into my files for examples of when there's been massive political involvement, if needed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T11:34:40-08:00","id":1002282,"title":"","content":"how difficult a blessing with soothsay Fatalism, or entropy, would &quot;Would win the Election&quot; be?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T12:18:07-08:00","id":1002301,"title":"","content":"well, that's the thing. you would need an army of awakened led by masters working on a major ritual to put an entropy effect big enough to alter the minds of several billion people. thats a lot of successes. you got to think smaller. subliminal mind effects delivered over years via talk radio to push people into the mindset you want them in. memes on the internet pushing boundaries of taste a little more in your favor. computer algorithms that suppress opposing views in social media battlefields. Umbral constructs that psychically reinforce trends and patterns. Storm Chasers pushing hurricanes to hit just the right coast to anger residents at the financially crippled emergency response time. round the clock efforts within a entrenched and zealous propaganda distribution network. investment of time and effort guided by enlightened insight and clarity of vision will overcome brute force magical effects, which is one of the main reasons that the traditions have been on the run for so long. and entropy effect applied to politics would be more wisely aimed at giving the candidate good luck during debates and public appearances. mind effects that clearly communicate their words to he audience and primal investments to cause their views to appear to have more value than their opponents. if it were so simple to cast a spell to be president then we would have had a very different historical record. of course if you go by 1st edition the technocrats have been engeneering elections and politics as the super illuminati that they are and its really all a battle between them the lizard people of england. but the point is that change takes dedicated effort even with magic in the mix and the powers that be will actively counter it directly or indirectly. don't think they aren't scanning the future for disruptions to their timetable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>there are no bad ideas, just ideas that have not been refined enough","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1608-iamthesweeper","name":"IAmTheSweeper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1608_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T15:16:45-08:00","id":1002378,"title":"","content":"Well, even if said election were the American Presidential Election, it wouldn't be the minds of several billion people. Two hundred million, at most, and probably not even that if we are talking just about american voters.<br /> <br /> That said, a luck effect alone would have a hard time doing this. It certainly can affect some aspects, and tip the balance a little. But you have to think how broad the election's structure is. A lot of the results are based mainly on direct intent from the voters, and luck effects can't affect that, it isn't random. Now, you could rig an election by other means, though it would probably be resisted by other interested parts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T15:22:35-08:00","id":1002379,"title":"","content":"A local sherrif or mayors election?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T17:30:13-08:00","id":1002404,"title":"","content":"also as for changelings, the Ailil will FREQUENTLY seek to work with politicians or business men, but even they are more likely to be mentors or puppet masters, not running for office themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T19:44:43-08:00","id":1002431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1000435-bit-of-a-controversial-subject-world-of-darkness-and-politics?p=1002379#post1002379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A local sherrif or mayors election?</div> </div> </div> </div>The same principles goes on, you just will have a less broad scope to deal with, but usually still big for your everyday magic.<br /> <br /> It isn't that a big election isn't based on luck. It is that no election is based on luck. They're elections. People are consciously making decisions about their votes, so you can't change those votes by changing luck. What a luck spell can do is to alter the random variables in the system, like events that can deter some people of voting, or lead them to do it, or the chance of some happenstance destroying the votes already deposited. But since too much of those happenstances would probably result in the entire process being cancelled out, there's not much room for luck playing any big role.<br /> <br /> Luck, and luck magic, would make for a difference only at very specific circumstances. Only two come to my mind: when the difference between the candidates is too little, so even a lesser tip in the balance can change everything. The other is when too much of the voters are unsure, so even chance events can made their minds enough in their way to the polls. You could try some very careful uses of luck magic to indirect affect the electoral campaign to make it more probable for people to see the best of candidate A and the worst of candidate B, but that would be a helluva hard and judicious use of such magic, even in a school's election.<br /> <br /> Only magic able to actually control people or affect the data could actually influence the elections with only one spell. You can enchant the place where the votes are deposited to physically change the papers, letting some unadulterated to avoid it becoming too obvious. Or you can Dominate a good proportion of voters, aiming at the ones you already know to be uninterested in voting for your side, so they do vote the way you want. On a specially tricky try, you can aim for someone who can alone change things greatly, like the opposing candidate proper, to do something that can alter the results.<br /> <br /> Mostly you should look for a long, mixed strategy. Use magic judiciously to affect things here and there, keep an eye at how people are intending to vote, look out for magical interference of other factions. It could take a good chunk of a chronicle to make something about an election. Mix magic with a lot of more physical groundwork. You can really read <b>IAmTheSweeper</b>'s post for ideas. The process is essentially the same for any poll, be it some sort of world-wide direct election, or simply a poll between 5 teenagers to decide the next event of the night.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T20:02:41-08:00","id":1002440,"title":"","content":"I did wind up having a little bit of a dig, and here are some very explicit and very major bits of interference - including a few that go against White Wolf's general policy re: purely human evils.<br /> One element that complicates the question is whether we should include cases where the actual <i>cause</i> of the action is unclear (e.g., how much of the oil policy in the Arab World in the early 1900s was down to the Technocracy and how much was down purely to human greed?) and where both sides are taking distinct but related actions that feed into each other without direct influence.<br /> <br /> In 1900, the Akashic Brotherhood openly backed the Boxer Rebellion.<br /> In 1909, Mathieu Hullebusch tried to openly overthrow the Belgian Congo's ruling government with his army of flying Etherite robots.<br /> 1914... Vargo's a weird one as he doesn't quite count, having been all but erased from history by paradox. But at the same time, Lodin is outright controlling the unions in Chicago.<br /> In 1915, the Virtual Adepts arrange for the Zimmerman Telegram to be sent. If they hadn't, it would have been sent in 1917. The exact impact of this isn't really clear - on paper it shouldn't have made a major difference except for making the war a little longer, but as we all know, one small event can quickly spiral out of control and two more years for possible Unexpected Events could radically reshape the situation in Mexico and the US enough to significantly alter their involvement or lack of in the War.<br /> In 1917, the Atlanta Fire is caused by spectres. It isn't quite a political event, but it has massive political consequences down the line by reshaping the political and personal landscape of the city.<br /> In the same year, as we all know the Brujah either rode along with the Russian Revolution or outright masterminded it, depending on which source you take.<br /> In 1918, America's involvement in the Russian Expeditionary Force is caused by Ventrue manipulation.<br /> In 1920, Spectres deliberately incite violence in Chicago's gangland. Again, not quite political - but the violence of the bootleggers also had major political consequences down the chain.<br /> Same year, Barbarossa and his Brujah back the Socialists in Frankfurt.<br /> In 1921, we get Lodin being an absolute cunt and destroying the economy of Gary, Indiana as a ploy against Modius. That must've taken him a while, too, since the economy there didn't collapse in our world until the 60s.<br /> 1924 had Trotskyite Brujah kill Lenin, and the Ventrue and Toreador put Stalin in charge.<br /> 1934 has the Tremere and Ventrue of Europe start backing Fascists to counter the Brujah-backed socialists and anarchists.<br /> 1939's Molotov-Ribbentrop pack is down to Brujah influence.<br /> 1940 sees - and this is the 'purely human evil' thing from earlier - Gustav Breidenstein start 'mentoring' Hitler. Now, the easy answer is 'retconned by Shoah!' But it was reprinted in the Encyclopedia Vampirica, which though written by the German licensee Feather and Sword was published in English by White Wolf in 2002. So not only does it significantly post-date Shoah, but it passed through White Wolf's translators and editors before being published, which means it's difficult to go 'well, it was just those licensees not getting the memo' on this one.<br /> WW2 generally sees big involvement by the Technocracy, but they're more piggybacking than engineering.<br /> 1941 is an exception, which is the Virtual Adepts engineering for Pearl Harbour to have any warnings ignored. They deliberately arrange for the high death toll of the attack in order to force America to action.<br /> The 1950s have repeated attempts by supernatural factions to trigger nuclear wars. Also not political, but I think it deserves a mention, no?<br /> 1959 sees the Cardona Ventrue join the Brujah Council to support Castro, basically ensuring the Revolution succeeds.<br /> In 1968, Lodin conspires to cause the DNC Riots. He uses them purely as a smokescreen for his own operation, but there are huge political ramifications from the act.<br /> In 1973, Barbarossa managed to make Frankfurt the home of the predecessor to the European Monetary Institute. That's definitely some International Politics right there.<br /> And that's only the first three-quarters of the 20th century. A lot of it can be put down to big talk by unreliable narrators, but at the same time, we can see that there's been plenty of involvement in regional, national, and international affairs and politics by all sorts of groups.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T08:17:44-08:00","id":1002894,"title":"","content":"oh wondered a bit, if a Changeling childling runs away from home to move in with their motley then a social worker comes to get them back... and they use either soveign or chicancery to send them off, how to make that a long term thing rather then to attract monster hunters, and tempory stopgap at best.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T12:05:51-08:00","id":1003000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1000435-bit-of-a-controversial-subject-world-of-darkness-and-politics?p=1002440#post1002440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did wind up having a little bit of a dig, and here are some very explicit and very major bits of interference - including a few that go against White Wolf's general policy re: purely human evils.<br /> One element that complicates the question is whether we should include cases where the actual <i>cause</i> of the action is unclear (e.g., how much of the oil policy in the Arab World in the early 1900s was down to the Technocracy and how much was down purely to human greed?) and where both sides are taking distinct but related actions that feed into each other without direct influence.<br /> <br /> In 1900, the Akashic Brotherhood openly backed the Boxer Rebellion.<br /> In 1909, Mathieu Hullebusch tried to openly overthrow the Belgian Congo's ruling government with his army of flying Etherite robots.<br /> 1914... Vargo's a weird one as he doesn't quite count, having been all but erased from history by paradox. But at the same time, Lodin is outright controlling the unions in Chicago.<br /> In 1915, the Virtual Adepts arrange for the Zimmerman Telegram to be sent. If they hadn't, it would have been sent in 1917. The exact impact of this isn't really clear - on paper it shouldn't have made a major difference except for making the war a little longer, but as we all know, one small event can quickly spiral out of control and two more years for possible Unexpected Events could radically reshape the situation in Mexico and the US enough to significantly alter their involvement or lack of in the War.<br /> In 1917, the Atlanta Fire is caused by spectres. It isn't quite a political event, but it has massive political consequences down the line by reshaping the political and personal landscape of the city.<br /> In the same year, as we all know the Brujah either rode along with the Russian Revolution or outright masterminded it, depending on which source you take.<br /> In 1918, America's involvement in the Russian Expeditionary Force is caused by Ventrue manipulation.<br /> In 1920, Spectres deliberately incite violence in Chicago's gangland. Again, not quite political - but the violence of the bootleggers also had major political consequences down the chain.<br /> Same year, Barbarossa and his Brujah back the Socialists in Frankfurt.<br /> In 1921, we get Lodin being an absolute cunt and destroying the economy of Gary, Indiana as a ploy against Modius. That must've taken him a while, too, since the economy there didn't collapse in our world until the 60s.<br /> 1924 had Trotskyite Brujah kill Lenin, and the Ventrue and Toreador put Stalin in charge.<br /> 1934 has the Tremere and Ventrue of Europe start backing Fascists to counter the Brujah-backed socialists and anarchists.<br /> 1939's Molotov-Ribbentrop pack is down to Brujah influence.<br /> 1940 sees - and this is the 'purely human evil' thing from earlier - Gustav Breidenstein start 'mentoring' Hitler. Now, the easy answer is 'retconned by Shoah!' But it was reprinted in the Encyclopedia Vampirica, which though written by the German licensee Feather and Sword was published in English by White Wolf in 2002. So not only does it significantly post-date Shoah, but it passed through White Wolf's translators and editors before being published, which means it's difficult to go 'well, it was just those licensees not getting the memo' on this one.<br /> WW2 generally sees big involvement by the Technocracy, but they're more piggybacking than engineering.<br /> 1941 is an exception, which is the Virtual Adepts engineering for Pearl Harbour to have any warnings ignored. They deliberately arrange for the high death toll of the attack in order to force America to action.<br /> The 1950s have repeated attempts by supernatural factions to trigger nuclear wars. Also not political, but I think it deserves a mention, no?<br /> 1959 sees the Cardona Ventrue join the Brujah Council to support Castro, basically ensuring the Revolution succeeds.<br /> In 1968, Lodin conspires to cause the DNC Riots. He uses them purely as a smokescreen for his own operation, but there are huge political ramifications from the act.<br /> In 1973, Barbarossa managed to make Frankfurt the home of the predecessor to the European Monetary Institute. That's definitely some International Politics right there.<br /> And that's only the first three-quarters of the 20th century. A lot of it can be put down to big talk by unreliable narrators, but at the same time, we can see that there's been plenty of involvement in regional, national, and international affairs and politics by all sorts of groups.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't that stuff all from the earlier 90s, when WW made Al Capone a vampire? If so, I would expect most of that to be moved into unreliable narrator stance if it isn't already.<br /> <br /> Expect for the Mage stuff, of course. Because Mage is difficult like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T12:15:08-08:00","id":1003003,"title":"","content":"Himmler was a vampire at some point, right? Oscar Wilde was a toreador with 8 intellegence. <br /> <br /> The stupidity...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Signatures are for terrible people who want to be caught.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12414-flower-innocent","name":"Flower,Innocent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T12:28:23-08:00","id":1003008,"title":"","content":"In 1935, blues musician Robert Johnson was Embraced by a Toreador and Huey Long was assassinated by order of the Syndicate. Source: GURPS Vampire and New Orleans by Night, respectively.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T16:42:08-08:00","id":1003134,"title":"","content":"As an almost completely side note, this thread survived 6 days, already.<br /> <br /> We are <u><b>really</b></u> civilized at this forum. I like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T18:19:00-08:00","id":1003181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1000435-bit-of-a-controversial-subject-world-of-darkness-and-politics?p=1003000#post1003000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Isn't that stuff all from the earlier 90s, when WW made Al Capone a vampire? If so, I would expect most of that to be moved into unreliable narrator stance if it isn't already.<br /> <br /> Expect for the Mage stuff, of course. Because Mage is difficult like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>A surprisingly large chunk of it is from later sources (e.g. the Brujah Council/Cardona Ventrue alliance being responsible for Castro's success is from 2002, the Pearl Harbour bit was affirmed in VA:Revised, and Mr. Hullebusch's valiant attempt to right the wrong in the Congo is revised era content) or was later affirmed in the Encyclopedia Vampirica, which is simultaneously meant to be a reliable source and an in-universe document. I did address the matter of unreliable narrators in the post itself, too.<br /> <br /> It's one of the tricky things about trying to establish a history of the setting. We have very little that can't be unreliable narrator'd away.<br /> <br /> As far as Capone goes, he's far from the most egregious figure to be made a vampire, nearly all from early VtM but some not. LEt's see... I have, from a very quick check of my database:<br /> Ambrose Bierce<br /> Oscar Wilde<br /> Louis Pasteur (now THAT one is the most early VtM of early VtM...)<br /> Aleister Crowley<br /> Squizzy Taylor<br /> <i>Jesus himself</i>. (he's a Lasombra, by the way.)<br /> Don Medina Sidonia<br /> <i>The actual Beowulf</i>.<br /> There's more but I'm still working on cleaning the database up.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T18:25:50-08:00","id":1003185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1000435-bit-of-a-controversial-subject-world-of-darkness-and-politics?p=1003134#post1003134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As an almost completely side note, this thread survived 6 days, already.<br /> <br /> We are <u><b>really</b></u> civilized at this forum. I like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>IM KNOCKING ON WOOD!!.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, the idea of Vampire Himmler was incredibly bad. i talked to RichT and he was a bit sadden and angry about it.<br /> <br /> personally, i like to imagine the supernaturals sending their ghouls to vote for a candidate . or worried about the elections, since it might interviene with their agendas","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T20:34:53-08:00","id":1003219,"title":"","content":"I only going to speak about VtM here as it is the one I have the most experience playing. I could easily see Kindred influencing local, state or provincial politics. These would have a much greater impact on them than national level politics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12656-lasombra99","name":"Lasombra99","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T21:07:33-08:00","id":1003228,"title":"","content":"For some other events of note from another quick skim of the timeline. I'm excluding events from early in prehistory because back then you had vampires ruling openly as kings and gods, the Impergium, etc. As a quick aside, unless we assume every narrator is extremely unreliable and that explicit 'OOC' dates are unreliable, the often repeated statement that VtM somehow requires a literalist Young Earth biblical creation (usually, in such arguments, said to be either 6,000YA or 7,000YA) fails automatically because of the preponderance of evidence from VtM of characters and events older than that (e.g. Kindred religions that date back 14,000 years in State of Grace, Alamut's construction in circa 7300BCE, Japeth Cappadocius's embrace circa 7225BCE, the stated age of the Ravnos antediluvian as being at least 10,000 years) let alone evidence from other splats and lines.<br /> <br /> 1152: Barbarossa's bid for the empire succeeded in large part thanks to the influence of Angiwar.<br /> 1202: The Giovanni manipulate the Doge of Venice into backing the 4th Crusade, with its known devastating consequences to mortal and cainite alike.<br /> 1356: Chu Yuan-Chang, a master of the Akashic order, seizes control of the Red Turban Rebellion and becomes the Hongwu Emperor. This may simply be Big Talk by the Akashics, but the reference for the event itself is a 2015 book - M20.<br /> 1381: Robin Leeland and his Brujah lend their muscle to Wat Tyler's peasant revolt. It's a direct attempt to use mortal politics to break supernatural politics, and it ultimately succeeds via Patricia of Bollingbroke's diablerie of Hardestadt permanently shattering the status quo of the Medieval Princes and the birth of the Camarilla. Of course, the Peasants' Revolt achieved basically fuckall in the end except some lower taxes over the rest of the Hundred Years War, even if it got lionized a lot for a while. Bit of a mixed bag, but hey - at least Leeland ultimately managed to shake things up.<br /> 1493: It isn't quite political, but it gets a mention. The reason the spread of disease in the contact between the Old and New World was so devastating was in part the work of the Ratkin. Of course, a cynical view is that they're just taking the credit for it and it would have happened anyway, but this was not presented as unreliable narrator material but as hard fact insofar as such a thing exists in the oWoD. Given that it fundamentally reshapes societies and opens up the New World as 'unsettled' land, it's a Big Deal.<br /> 1522: Etrius is behind Ferdinand I's 'Bloody Trials'.<br /> 1611: Polish Tzimisce directly instigate the Polish invasion of Russia.<br /> <br /> That's just a few, and only events that are directly attributable to supernatural influence (with the exception of the peasants' revolt) rather than where it's been exploited but not caused.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}